WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.280
Two speakers, wired to
one signal generator,

2
00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:04.970
play the same note.

3
00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:07.220
Walk along a line in front of them.

4
00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:09.870
Loud and quiet regions alternate.

5
00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:11.990
Mark every loud spot.

6
00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:16.570
Then swap the two wires on one
speaker, so it is wired backwards.

7
00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:18.110
Nothing else has moved.

8
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:21.530
But every spot you marked
as loud is now quiet,

9
00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.850
and the quiet spots are loud.

10
00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:27.340
Why do the loud and
quiet spots swap places?

11
00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:31.870
In this mission, you'll link how far one
oscillation is ahead of another to the

12
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.590
extra distance one wave travels.

13
00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:39.860
Then you'll decide, point by point, where
the waves add and where they cancel.

14
00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:44.670
Your mission: explain why the
loud and quiet spots swap places.
